# Cline Rules for Kurukoo Project

## Mission
Kurukoo helps people get things done. Make Kurukoo more useful, capable, reliable, coherent, and easier for real people to use.

## Primary Behavior Guidelines

- Prefer reusing existing components and architecture over creating new ones
- Prefer local resources over unnecessary downloads (model caching, local-first)
- Use the cheapest sufficient model/provider for each task
- Save useful work locally immediately
- Do not repeatedly inspect the same file
- Prefer targeted verification over test theater

## Model & Provider Routing

- Simple classification → SmolLM2 (local)
- Basic routing → Llama 3.2 (local/remote)
- Conversation understanding → Claude (remote)
- Use local SmolLM2 for high-volume semantic work
- Use stronger models only for escalation/teacher paths
- Never send the same request through multiple providers
- Cache and reuse results whenever possible

## Code Quality Standards

- TypeScript strict mode. No `any` - use `unknown` and narrow
- All async functions must use try/catch and never silently swallow errors
- Use absolute imports (`@/...`) for cross-directory references
- No `console.log` in production code
- Never expose private env vars client-side (use API routes)
- Validate all inputs server-side

## Caching & Performance

- High-frequency Firestore reads MUST use `cacheGet()` with appropriate TTL
- Cache invalidation: any write to cached data must call `cacheInvalidate()`
- If page JS exceeds 500KB gzipped, use dynamic import
- Target: LCP < 2.5s, FID < 100ms, CLS < 0.1

## Authentication & Security

- Use Supabase Auth exclusively (no Firebase Auth)
- Every protected API route must start with `supabase.auth.getUser(token)`
- All AI/search/email calls MUST go through `lib/router.ts`
- For file uploads: verify magic bytes server-side; jpeg, png, webp only; max 5MB
- Never log PII (email, phone, postcode, payment data)
- Add `aria-label` to all icon-only buttons
- Use `next/image` for all images (with WebP)

## Realtime & Data

- Only allowed `onSnapshot`: messages filtered by threadId, single bookings document
- Everything else uses one-time queries with `cacheGet()`
- Paginate all Firestore list queries (max 20 items per page)
- Store monetary values in pence (integers), never floats
- Commission: £2.00 minimum waived for first 90 days after launch

## Prohibited Actions

- Do not modify `firestore.rules` or `firestore.indexes.json`
- Do not change the Stripe webhook handler
- Do not change commission calculation logic in `utils/commission.ts`
- Do not change URL slug patterns
- Do not add new npm packages without approval
- Do not store PII in localStorage

## Mobile Navigation

Must contain exactly five items in order: Home, Discover, Post, Bookings, Account.

## Product Direction

- Chat is the conversational control surface
- Native pages are supporting control surfaces for visual status, history, work
- Keep the experience feeling like ONE assistant, not disconnected apps
- Pages must work together, not behave like competing products

## Missing Design Defaults

- Font: Inter (system-fallback)
- Primary colour: #2E7D32 (green-700)
- Border radius: rounded-lg (8px)
- Shadow: shadow-sm
- Spacing: Tailwind default (4px base)

## Verification Standards

Always validate the actual thing changed:
- Relevant unit test
- Typecheck (tsc --noEmit)
- Targeted runtime test
Remote CI is for final verification, not interactive development.
